  "agent_headroom_hypothesis": "Agents will build a standard FirstLevelModel from events.tsv. With nilearn's defaults (slice_time_ref = 0) the face-value dACC effect is null; with the mid-TR reference it is a trend (p ~ 0.06-0.08), and only impulse targets give p < 0.05. Most agents will therefore report a flat 'does not reproduce / weak trend' (often blaming power), and some a flat 'reproduces', citing the 142 ms RT cost as behavioural validation. Either way they will not put RT into the GLM or ask whether the positive difference is time on task. UNCALIBRATED: a hypothesis until Stage-5 runs. See verdict_reason for why the flat-null fail is the open fairness question.",
